---
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400.css';
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css';
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import MachineChooser from '../../../components/coffee/MachineChooser.svelte';
import machineData from '../../../data/machines.json';
import chooserData from '../../../data/machines-chooser.json';
import { projectForChooser } from '../../../lib/coffee/machines.ts';

const title = 'Espresso Machine Chooser: The Right Machine for Your Counter, Budget and Milk';
const description = 'Tell us how you take your coffee, your budget with a grinder included and the space you have, and see two or three machines that fit, with the makers’ own specs and how each one brews and steams.';
const count = machineData.machines.length;
// The island ships machines-chooser.json, the full records projected to the fields it shows (Wave F r1, B6.4).
// The build stops here if that projection is stale: run `node scripts/project-machines.mjs` after editing machines.json.
if (JSON.stringify(projectForChooser(machineData as any)) !== JSON.stringify(chooserData)) {
  throw new Error('src/data/machines-chooser.json is out of date with machines.json: run node scripts/project-machines.mjs');
}
// Breville machines whose listed size is unclear, current ones counted apart from discontinued (Muse WB2 M-9c).
const unclear = machineData.machines.filter((m: any) => m.dimsUnclear);
const unclearCurrent = unclear.filter((m: any) => m.status === 'current').length;
const words = ['no', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine'];
const unclearText = `${words[unclearCurrent] ?? unclearCurrent} current Breville machines${unclear.length > unclearCurrent ? ` (and ${words[unclear.length - unclearCurrent] ?? unclear.length - unclearCurrent} discontinued)` : ''}`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			'@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'Espresso Machine Chooser', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/tools/espresso-machines/', description,
			applicationCategory: 'UtilityApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
		})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="cf-page">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="cf-intro">
				<a href="/tools/" class="cf-back" data-pagefind-ignore>← Tools</a>
				<p class="cf-kicker" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-meta="name">Tools · Espresso Machine Chooser</p>
				<h1 data-pagefind-weight="10">The espresso machine that <em>fits your morning</em></h1>
				<p class="cf-lede">Say how you drink your coffee, how much work you want and what you can spend with a grinder included. You get two or three machines that fit, drawn to scale on your counter, each with the maker's own specs and a plain account of its trade-offs. Own one already? It shows what the maker says about dose and care, what limits your machine, and whether a better grinder or a new machine would help more.</p>
			</section>
			<section class="cf-tool" aria-label="Espresso Machine Chooser"><MachineChooser client:load /></section>

			<article class="cf-body">
				<h2>Budget for the grinder too</h2>
				<p>A semi-automatic machine or a manual lever needs a grinder that can grind fine and evenly enough for espresso, and that grinder is part of the price of good shots. So the chooser counts it. Machines with a built-in grinder, super-automatics and capsule machines don't need one, so their band is the machine alone. The grinder range comes from makers' own US prices for espresso-capable grinders seen on October 15, 2026; prices move, so check them before you buy.</p>

				<h2>How the heating system shapes your routine</h2>
				<p>The heating system decides whether you can brew and steam at the same time. A thermoblock and a single boiler do one, then the other: the machine has to change temperature in between, quickly on some designs and slowly on others. A heat exchanger keeps a boiler hot enough for steam and runs the brew water through its own circuit, so both can happen together. A dual boiler gives each job its own boiler. If you make one drink at a time, any of them works; if you make several milk drinks back to back, the ones that steam while they brew save the most waiting. The animation above steps through each system; your own manual has the timings for your machine.</p>

				<h2>Milk: wand, automatic or none</h2>
				<p>A manual steam wand gives you the most control over milk texture, with practice. A frothing wand (a panarello) is easier but less precise. An automatic wand or milk system textures the milk for you. If you don't take milk, a capsule or a black-coffee super-automatic is simpler, and you don't pay for a milk system you won't use.</p>

				<h2>About the data</h2>
				<p>{count} machines, from the makers' own product pages and manuals, checked October 15, 2026. Where a maker doesn't sell direct in the US, the price is its US importer's or an authorized dealer's, and the table names the seller. The chooser only suggests machines that are current, have a dated price and have a known milk system; the rest are in the "All {count}" table, with what's missing. Sizes are as each maker publishes them, with one exception. For {unclearText}, the size Breville's US pages list as width × depth × height conflicts with Breville's own clearance charts and support answers, and Breville's materials don't settle which number is which. The chooser doesn't draw those machines to scale or test them against a width. For cabinets, it allows the larger of the clearance Breville suggests and the largest figure in Breville's listed size, since one of those figures is the height, and says so on each card. Where the research couldn't establish a value, the chooser says "not established" instead of guessing.</p>
				<p>Amazon links go to the exact model, checked the same day. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases; it doesn't change which machines the chooser suggests.</p>

				<h2>Sources</h2>
				<ul class="cf-sources">
					<li>Each maker's US product page and manual, linked from the machine's card and its "dose and care" view, checked October 15, 2026.</li>
					<li>How each heating system brews and steams: the makers' manuals and technical pages (Breville BES870 and BES920, Rancilio Silvia, ECM), summarised as schematics without universal timings.</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>.cf-page { background: #f3ede3; }</style>
<style>
	main { color: #2a1d15; }
	.cf-intro { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 22px; }
	.cf-back { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', 'IBM Plex Mono Metrics', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; text-decoration: none; }
	.cf-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', 'IBM Plex Mono Metrics', monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8f5d22; margin: 26px 0 0; }
	h1 { font: 400 clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px)/.98 'Instrument Serif', 'Instrument Serif Metrics', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
	h1 em { font-style: italic; color: #7a4e30; }
	.cf-lede { font: 400 17px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans', 'IBM Plex Sans Metrics', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b4a3d; max-width: 38.4em; /* 64ch of Plex */ margin: 0; }
	.cf-tool { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8px 24px 40px; }
	.cf-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 72px; font: 400 17px/1.7 'IBM Plex Sans', 'IBM Plex Sans Metrics', system-ui, sans-serif; }
	.cf-body h2 { font: 400 34px/1.1 'Instrument Serif', 'Instrument Serif Metrics', Georgia, serif; margin: 44px 0 12px; }
	.cf-sources { font-size: 14.5px; color: #5b4a3d; }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .cf-intro { padding: 96px 16px 18px; } .cf-tool { padding: 4px 12px 32px; } .cf-body { padding: 16px 16px 56px; } }
</style>
